   "entry.freeform.source_name": "Pasted program",
   "entry.freeform.prompt": "Rewrite this training program as JSON for the Taurifer app. Reply with the JSON and nothing else: no explanation, no code fences.\n\nUse exactly this shape:\n{\"version\":3,\"meta\":{\"name\":\"Program name\"},\"exercises\":[{\"day\":\"Day label\",\"order\":1,\"name\":\"Exercise name\",\"sets\":3,\"min\":6,\"max\":10}],\"missing\":[],\"notImported\":[]}\n\nRules:\n- Preserve exercise selection, order, day grouping and names exactly as the source writes them, in the source's language.\n- One entry per exercise per training day. Repeat \"day\" on every exercise in that day, and number \"order\" from 1 within each day.\n- \"sets\" is the number of working sets, a whole number from 1 to 100.\n- \"min\" and \"max\" are the rep range as whole numbers. Where the source gives one rep number, use it for both bounds.\n- Never substitute an exercise, never redesign, never invent a day, an exercise, a set count or a rep range.\n- Where a required value is genuinely absent, omit the field and name it in \"missing\": [{\"day\":\"Day label\",\"order\":1,\"field\":\"sets\"|\"reps\"}]. Do not guess it, and do not ask a question; return the structure.\n- Name anything the source carried that this shape cannot hold in \"notImported\", using only these categories: \"rest_times\", \"rir_rpe\", \"tempo\", \"supersets\", \"warmups\", \"cardio\", \"progression_rules\", \"deload\", \"other_notes\".\n- Leave out warm-ups, cardio and anything that is not a working exercise.\n\nThe program:\n\n{program}",
